Since the optical depth for photon-photon pair creation is around unity, the TeV photons created via the synchrotron-self-Compton process cannot be easily absorbed by the magnetospheric IR-UV photons, as indicated by the dashed and thick solid curves in figure 5. It suggests that we may expect relatively strong pulsed emissions around TeV from the pulsars of which inverse-Compton and photon-photon-absorption optical depths are around unity, which is typical for young pulsars with ages around several thousand years. We will discuss this possibility in a separate paper.

